This product is a derivative work: its Unity format handling is hand-ported
from the projects below. Their copyright notices are kept per the MIT License,
and every ported source file carries a one-line attribution to the file it was
ported from.

AssetStudio -- https://github.com/Razviar/assetstudio (MIT)
  Copyright (c) Perfare, RazTools, Razviar
  Source of truth for AssetBundle, SerializedFile, TypeTree and class layout.

UnityPy -- https://github.com/K0lb3/UnityPy (MIT)
  Copyright (c) K0lb3
  Oracle used to generate the test goldens, and behaviour source where it and
  AssetStudio disagree: the UnityFS header version gates in
  src/bundle/BundleFile.ts are ported from its files/BundleFile.py; the
  common strings past AssetStudio's Hash128 in src/serialized/CommonString.ts
  come from the TPK table behind its helpers/Tpk.py; and
  src/serialized/TypeTreeReader.ts ports its [SerializeReference] ref type
  lookup and registry reading from its helpers/TypeTreeHelper.py. Format-23
  type-tree metadata and blob headers in src/serialized/TypeTree.ts come from
  its files/SerializedFile.py and helpers/TypeTreeNode.py (UnityPy 1.25.4).

Runtime dependencies are external (see package.json): dist/ keeps the import and
npm installs them, so their own LICENSE files ship with them and no copy of
their code is distributed inside this package (plan section 2, #71).
